  "customHelp": "VELOCITY CARD GAME — DIGITAL PLAYTEST\n\nOBJECTIVE\nScore 10 Victory Points before your opponent by the end of regulation. A match is played over two halves. If tied after regulation, each player receives one overtime turn; if still tied, play sudden death until a player scores.\n\nPRE-GAME\nPlace your Head Coach. Determine the starting player. The die-roll/coin-flip winner selects and places the Arena for the match. Set five Starters in the Frontline: 1 Franchise, 1 Star, 2 Role Players, and 1 Veteran. Set up to five Bench players. Shuffle the Playbook and draw 5 cards.\n\nTURN PHASES\n1. Start Phase — draw 1 card, adjust Momentum as required, resolve start/passive effects.\n2. Main Phase — play Events, make substitutions, activate eligible abilities.\n3. Play Phase — resolve the scoring attempt.\n4. End Phase — resolve end effects and pass the turn.\n\nACTION LIMIT\nA player may use at most 1 Offensive Action, 1 Defensive Action, and 1 Generic Action during the applicable timing windows of a turn. Effects that explicitly say otherwise override this restriction.\n\nPLAY PHASE\nOffensive Step: total the Skill of all five offensive Starters and resolve eligible Offensive/Generic Actions and abilities.\nDefensive Response: defender may use its Defensive Action, eligible Generic Action, and abilities.\nOffensive Response: offense may respond with 1 Defensive Action and/or eligible abilities; it may not play another Offensive Action.\nSkill Calculation: compare Final Team Skill after all modifiers.\nIf offense wins, it scores 1 VP and assigns Fatigue equal to the Skill difference among the defending Starters. If defense wins, no VP is scored and the defender assigns Fatigue equal to the Skill difference among the offensive Starters.\nExact ties should be resolved according to the current agreed playtest ruling; TCGA does not automate this result.\n\nFATIGUE / INJURY\nTrack Fatigue on the individual Player card. When accumulated Fatigue reaches the printed Fatigue limit (or the player's remaining Fatigue is reduced to 0 under the current card wording), that Player is Injured and is moved to Discard. A Starter who is Injured must be replaced by an eligible Bench player when required by the rules.\n\nHALFTIME\nAt halftime, perform the roster/deck changes permitted by the current Velocity rules, including eligible Reserve substitutions and Playbook side-deck changes.\n\nDIGITAL NOTE\nTCG Arena is being used as a manual rules simulator. Card text, Skill modifiers, Fatigue assignment, triggers, substitutions, Momentum spending, and timing decisions are resolved by the players unless specifically automated by the platform.",
